---
title: "One sticky note: typing, saving, outside edits, archive and Trash"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: syncing
    lg1: stored
    lg2: Breaks PurgeRespectsRetention or TypedTextKept in some cases
    lg3: Path to the PurgeRespectsRetention or TypedTextKept bug
    state "Terms" as terms {
      direction TB
      state " " as tc0 {
        direction LR
        tm0: person = The owner, using Sticky Notes on this Mac.
        tm1: save timer = The half-second pause after typing before the note is written to its file.
        tm2: file watcher = The part of the app that notices the note's file changed on disk.
        tm3: outside edit = A change to the note's file made by Obsidian, the other Mac or iCloud.
      }
      state " " as tc1 {
        direction LR
        tm4: conflict version = A second copy of the file that iCloud keeps when two saves disagree.
        tm5: conflict sweep = The app step that merges conflict versions back into the file and appends a 'Conflicted copy' section.
        tm6: other Mac = The owner's second Mac, running Sticky Notes on the same vault.
        tm7: Obsidian = The notes app that shares the vault folder.
      }
      state " " as tc2 {
        direction LR
        tm8: iCloud = iCloud Drive, which syncs the vault between the Macs.
        tm9: archive = Closed notes, still listed in the notes panel.
        tm10: Trash = Notes deleted from the archive, kept 30 days.
      }
    }
  }
  class lg0 orange
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 mayBreak
  class lg3 bugPath
  s0: File changed, window not told yet
  s1: Typing, save pending
  s2: Note in the archive
  s3: Note in the Trash
  s4: App quit, note on disk
  s5: Note file deleted
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: the person types in the note
  s0 --> s0: the calendar moves past the 30-day retention
  s1 --> s2: the person clicks the note's close button [the note has text]
  s0 --> s3: the person leaves an empty note by closing it or switching away
  s2 --> s2: the calendar moves past the 30-day retention
  s3 --> s4: the person quits the app
  s4 --> s5: the person launches the app
  s2 --> s3: the person deletes the note permanently
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
  class s0 orange
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 orange
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 teal
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 teal
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 teal
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 teal
  class s5 mayBreak
  class s5 bugPath
